{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310811,"nonce":"u5JvB3cMiCWKxJDr7CLhIFNbhgc=","title":"MEASURED 2026-08-04: nue's SpeculativeGenerationLoop (prompt-lookup, already implemented) is a NET LOSS — decode 7.5 -\u003e 4.2/2.4 tok/s, 2/2 ...","message":"**User: \"Haven't we explored this many times and keep backtracking?\"** Yes — and\nthe reason is now fixed: it was BUILT, NEVER MEASURED, and I kept nominating it\nwithout checking HEAD ([[feedback_dont_reiterate_closed_blockers]] says verify\nfirst; I broke that twice).\n\n`nue/nue/sampling/SpeculativeGenerationLoop.hx` — 347 lines, **prompt-lookup**\n(no draft model): finds a matching n-gram in the already-tokenised\nprompt/output, drafts the continuation, verifies with ONE batched target\nforward, rewinds the KV cache on mismatch. Wired into `Conversation` behind\n`GenerationConfig.useSpeculative` (default FALSE), toggled by\n`NUE_SPEC_DECODE=1`, stats via `RAYZOR_SPEC_PROFILE=1`, tuned by\n`RAYZOR_SPEC_MAX` (draft len, 4) and `RAYZOR_SPEC_NGRAM` (4).\n\nPage cache warmed first, cache swept + `--no-cache` per arm, interleaved:\n\n| | decode off | decode on |\n|---|---|---|\n| pair 1 | **7.48 tok/s** | 4.18 tok/s |\n| pair 2 | **7.15 tok/s** | 2.43 tok/s |\n\n**1.8-2.9x SLOWER, 2/2 pairwise. Keep it OFF (it already is).**\n\n    [profile-spec] batches=2 drafted=6 accepted=2 rejected=2 fallback=42\n                   disabled=0 accept_pct=33.3\n\n`batches=2, fallback=42` — across 48 tokens the n-gram lookup matched TWICE and\ndrafted 6 tokens total. It barely engages, yet decode still collapses 2-3x.\nSo the loss is in the loop's own per-step path (taken 42/48 times), not in\nwasted verification.\n\n**Leading hypothesis, UNTESTED: the fallback misses the `batch == 1` decode\nfast path in `Q4Matmul.matmul()`** and takes the banded path instead — that\nwould explain a multiple rather than a margin. Check what shape the\nspeculative loop hands to `forward` on a fallback step.\n\nSecond finding: the lookup failed 42/48 times on a prompt that is the SAME\n55-token passage repeated 13 times. If prompt-lookup cannot find drafts there,\nit will not in ordinary chat. Either `ngram=4` matching is too strict / buggy,\nor the model's output simply does not echo the prompt.\n\n**Speculative decode is NOT the next lever and should not be proposed as one\nagain without new evidence.** Two separate things would have to be fixed first:\n(1) the per-step overhead that costs 2-3x even when idle, and (2) an acceptance\nrate high enough to pay — currently it engages 4% of steps.\n\nThe batched-decode ARGUMENT still stands on its own (it would monetise the q4\nheader hoist and q6 tile inversion, which only fire at batch\u003e1) — but this\nimplementation does not deliver it.\n\n- `trace(\"[profile-spec] ...\")` is behind `if (profile)` = `RAYZOR_SPEC_PROFILE`.\n  A first run without it produced timings with no way to tell whether the\n  mechanism engaged at all.\n- First attempt was also confounded by COLD PAGE CACHE: TTFT 4.95s vs 1.43s for\n  an identical short prompt, purely because one arm loaded the 4 GB model\n  first. **Warm the model with a throwaway run before any decode A/B.**\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_speculative_decode_measured_net_loss` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}